//C& EDUCATION⁠
⁠
The Broad Museum has invited African American poet Aja Monet to recite poems as part of "When the Earth is a Hand Written Letter From the Past," in tribute to this year's #Juneteenth. "Every Media Minute," "The Devil You Know," and "Untitled" are each contributing to the audiovisual repertoire of this critical discourse, paired with the works of David Hammons and Hank Willis Thomas. These narratives intertwine, aiming to investigate the racial history of the United States, the Civil Rights Movement, and their ties to various social and political movements.⁠
@ajamonet⁠
@hankwillisthomas⁠
@thebroadmuseum⁠
⁠
Dive into the 9-minute video, where Monet confronts stereotypes, advocates for rights, and reveals the politics embedded in American life. From the power of collective action to the plight of impoverished communities, she weaves a narrative where the EARTH is the protagonist, reminding us that the most important choice lies in the heart.⁠
⁠
Check out the video via LINK IN BIO.⁠
